1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,778
Verdict Picks Toon: The Robot That Can't See You

2
00:00:01,928 --> 00:00:05,969
Black Friday week. 11:48 p.m. Robot vacuums are on sale. Goodbye, dog hair!

3
00:00:06,119 --> 00:00:10,694
2022: photos taken by test robot vacuums were posted online (MIT Technology Review). 2026: hacked robots showed live camera feeds (Tom's Hardware).

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:13,267
Wait. My vacuum would have a CAMERA?

5
00:00:13,417 --> 00:00:16,266
Many robots dodge clutter by photographing it.

6
00:00:16,416 --> 00:00:20,991
There's another way: a spinning laser. LiDAR. It measures distance. It never takes a photo.

7
00:00:21,141 --> 00:00:23,862
It maps your home in the dark. No pictures.

8
00:00:24,012 --> 00:00:26,351
Then no camera, no problem! Mostly.

9
00:00:26,501 --> 00:00:30,329
It scans at the height of its turret. It sees the sofa, not the sock.

10
00:00:30,479 --> 00:00:35,054
CNET lab test, November 13, 2026: Camera-free Roomba 205 Combo avoided 1 of 6; Roomba Combo 10 Max (camera) avoided 6 of 6 Source: CNET, best robot vacuums of 2026 (lab test by Ajay Kumar).

11
00:00:35,204 --> 00:00:38,904
And no camera-free robot in our guide promises to avoid pet waste.

12
00:00:39,054 --> 00:00:40,754
BISCUIT IS A PUPPY!

13
00:00:40,904 --> 00:00:45,479
Which robot for your home?: Tidy floor, privacy first no camera; Puppy, sick pet, cords camera robot

14
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:50,203
Next morning. The 30-second rule: cords and socks off the floor before every run. Floor's clear, buddy. Let's go.

15
00:00:50,353 --> 00:00:54,928
One more thing: a laser robot still sends your floor map to the cloud. Skip the data-sharing program in the app. No photos. Just us.

16
00:00:55,078 --> 00:00:57,197
Which camera-free robot should you buy? Six picks, compared below. Link in description.

